     1,
     "<p style=\"font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,arial,helvetica,sans-serif;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;border:0px;outline:0px;font-size:13.333332px;word-break:break-word;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Hello everyone,</p><p style=\"font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,arial,helvetica,sans-serif;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;border:0px;outline:0px;font-size:13.333332px;word-break:break-word;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">I need help with this. </p><p style=\"font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,arial,helvetica,sans-serif;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;border:0px;outline:0px;font-size:13.333332px;word-break:break-word;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">I ran RSF on my manatee dataset, and now I&#39;m struggling to plot response curves for my covariates. I used the &quot;intensity&quot; function for some individuals, but it&#39;s not working for my population-mean model.<br></p><p style=\"font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,arial,helvetica,sans-serif;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;border:0px;outline:0px;font-size:13.333332px;word-break:break-word;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Does anyone know how to plot these response curves using the information stored in the ctmm RSF object (.rda)?<br><br></p><p style=\"font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,arial,helvetica,sans-serif;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;border:0px;outline:0px;font-size:13.333332px;word-break:break-word;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Thanks a lot!</p><p style=\"font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,arial,helvetica,sans-serif;margin:0px 0px 1em;padding:0px;border:0px;outline:0px;font-size:13.333332px;word-break:break-word;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-size:13.333332px\">Iran Normande </span><br></p>"
    ]
